{# The raised choice in a segmented control -- every .ds-segmented, the
   toolbar's sections among them -- slides to the next rather than
   jumping. It is a thumb the group draws behind its items (ds.css), put
   under whichever item is chosen: aria-current="page" for a group of
   links, aria-pressed="true" for a group of buttons, or .is-selected.

   It moves when the choice does, whoever changes it: a page's own script
   pressing a tab, the toolbar marking the section being gone to
   (oeeeMarkCurrent), or a press here on a link in a page's pill, which is
   marked chosen at once and switched to in place, the pill left as it is
   (pill_macro.jinja). Anything else that moves the items -- a page
   arriving, a font loading, the window resizing, a menu opening on a group
   that was hidden -- puts it in place without sliding.

   The script is frontend/site/thumbs.ts. The boost swaps the body and runs
   the line below again, which places the new page's groups; the document's
   listeners are added once. #}
<script>if (window.oeeeChrome) window.oeeeChrome.thumbs();</script>
